SNOS is meant to be my OS project built from handwritten tools. The general
roadmap:

[ ]	lilhex[0]	A simple program to take a source file of hexadecimal
			values (and comments) and output a raw binary, from
			stdin to stdout.
[ ]	lilhex[1]	A port of lilhex[0] alongside the ability to define
			values and use them in a term to declare the value,
			name resolution occurs as a list of where each value
			is stored. Basic expressions may be used in the
			*declaration* of these expressions.
[ ]	lilhex[2]	lilhex[1] including a small parameter stack and the
			capacity to chain expressions together to determine
			declaration values with a simpler construction.
			Procedures may be created and executed wholly within
			lilhex[2].
[ ]	as[0]		May create a simple elf64 program with a single segment
			whose type is defined at the top of the input program,
			with a limited instruction set, allowing direct byte
			output with DB.
